  "question": {
    "text": "Light of wavelength $550 \\mathrm{~nm}$ falls normally on a slit of width $22.0 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~cm}$. The angular position of the second minima from the central maximum will be (in radians)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "unwjO",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{8}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "nbXKa",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{12}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OHXHq",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JSIdZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If angular position of $2^{\\text {nd }}$ maxima from central maxima is $\\theta$ then\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\sin \\theta=\\frac{(2 \\mathrm{n}-1) \\lambda}{2 \\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{3 \\lambda}{2 \\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{3 \\times 550 \\times 10^{-9}}{2 \\times 22 \\times 10^{-7}} \\\\\n&\\therefore \\quad \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{8} \\mathrm{rad}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
